{title: 385 - Crowning Jewel of Creation}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #385 • JEWEL • 13.15.12}
{lyricist: Gem Fitch}
{composer: Wayne Hooper}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 385}
{meta: tune JEWEL}
{meta: meter 13.15.12}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]Crowning jewel of creation, Blest and [Db]hallowed, [Ab/C]sanctified;
[Ab]Time and changes [Db]all [Eb7/Db]transcending, Shared [Ab]forever, [Eb/Bb]glori [Fm]fied.
[Db/F]Blessed Sabbath made [Eb7/Db]for [Ab/C]man, [Bbm]Gift [Eb]from [Ab]the Crea tor's hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Ab]Blessed Sabbath [Db]made [Cm]for [Fm]man,
[Eb7]Gift from the Creator's [Ab]hand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Sin and sickness, prayer and [Db]weeping
[Ab]Cease at [Eb7/Db]close of [Ab]earthly days;
[Ab]But Thy [Db]Sabbath [Eb7]is [Ab]eternal,
[Db/F]Joyful [Eb7/Db]thanks [Ab/C]to [Eb]Thee [Ab]we raise!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]Teach us Lord, in storm or [Db]sunshine
[Ab]How to [Eb7/Db]truly [Ab]rest [Cm]in [Ab]Thee,
[Ab]May Thy [Db]Sabbath [Eb7]peace [Ab]enfold us
[Db/F]And [Ab/Eb]our [Eb7/Db]shelter [Eb]ever [Ab]be.
{end_of_verse}
